# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

## Summary
Successfully verified and completed the installation of Vercel Speed Insights for this Next.js project.

## What Was Done

### 1. Installation
- Ran `npm install` to install the `@vercel/speed-insights` package (version 1.3.1)
- Package was already listed in package.json but needed to be installed
- Updated package-lock.json to lock the dependency versions

### 2. Configuration
The SpeedInsights component was already properly configured in the project:
- **File Modified**: `app/layout.tsx` (already had the correct implementation)
- **Import**: Using `@vercel/speed-insights/next` (correct for Next.js 15.1.11 with App Router)
- **Placement**: Component is placed inside the `<body>` tag after `{children}`, following best practices
- **No additional changes needed**: The implementation already follows Vercel's recommended setup

### 3. Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
- ✅ Static export generated without errors
- ✅ All 8 routes exported properly
- ✅ TypeScript compilation passed
- ✅ No runtime errors detected

## Technical Details

**Project Structure:**
- Next.js version: 15.1.11 (App Router)
- Package manager: npm
- Export mode: Static export (`output: 'export'`)
- Speed Insights version: 1.3.1

**Implementation Pattern:**
```typescript
import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next"

export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body>
        {children}
        <SpeedInsights />
      </body>
    </html>
  )
}
```

This implementation automatically tracks Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS, FCP, TTFB) and sends the data to Vercel's analytics dashboard when deployed.

## Files Changed
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with installed dependencies

## Notes
- The Speed Insights component was already implemented correctly in the codebase
- The main task was to ensure dependencies were properly installed
- No code changes were required as the implementation already followed best practices
- The component will automatically start collecting data when the site is deployed to Vercel
